{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781582244,"nonce":"j/0PjAzghScvkyMzgdeg7UDY/Kg=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFmiVUg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/280","origin":"github"},"title":"bizzyboat: record M3 .all files alongside sonar bags","message":"## Summary\n\nEnable the new `kongsberg_em_bridge` `.all` recording option on BizzyBoat so the\nM3 multibeam's raw Kongsberg EM datagram stream is archived as genuine `.all`\nfiles (loadable by Caris/Qimera/MB-System), saved alongside the sonar bags.\n\n## Background\n\n`rolker/marine_tools#46` (merged) added a `save_all_dir` parameter to\n`kongsberg_em_bridge`: when set, the node writes every received datagram to a\ntimestamped `m3_\u003cUTC\u003e.all` in that directory. Currently BizzyBoat's\n`perception_launch.py` launches the bridge without it, so nothing is recorded.\n\n## Change\n\nIn `bizzyboat_project11/launch/perception_launch.py`, pass `save_all_dir` to the\n`kongsberg_em_bridge` node, deriving the path from the existing\n`sonar_log_directory` (the `P11_SONAR_LOG_DIR` base, default\n`/home/field/data/logs/bizzyboat_sonar`) so the `.all` files land alongside the\nsonar bag recordings.\n\nUse a dedicated `m3_all/` subdirectory of the sonar log base rather than the\nper-session bag directory itself: the `sonar_logger` rosbag2 recorder writes to\n`\u003cbase\u003e/\u003ctimestamp\u003e` and errors if that directory already exists, so the bridge\n(which `makedirs` its save dir) must not create that path or its session parent.\n`\u003cbase\u003e/m3_all/` is a collision-free sibling of the bag directories.\n\nCross-repo: `rolker/marine_tools#46`.","files":null}]}